# Hansa coding-agent entry point - integrated 2026-10-24

## Read order
1. Read `docs/agent-reference/START_HERE.md` for authority, current context and scope.
2. Initial onboarding: read `docs/agent-reference/HANSA_MASTER_AGENT_REFERENCE_v1.0.md` in full once.
3. Structure, navigation, search, UX/accessibility or reorganization: read `docs/agent-reference/Hansa_Master_Audit_Reorganization_Plan_v2_2026-10-24.md`. Findings are dated evidence to recheck; target routes are proposals.
4. Charts, simulations, visual interactions, animations or library selection: read `docs/agent-reference/HANSA_ADAPTIVE_VISUALIZATION_AGENT_POLICY.md` in full on initial use.
5. New/revised pages: use `docs/agent-reference/CONTENT_BRIEF_TEMPLATE.yaml`. Candidate discovery: `docs/agent-reference/CAPABILITY_ROUTER.yaml` v1.1, never fixed library assignments.
6. Focused follow-ups: read affected sources, tests, decisions and relevant guide sections. Re-onboard when active references materially change.

## Authority and required behavior
The current owner request controls scope. Inspected repository/content facts describe reality; original sources govern factual claims. The v2 audit governs reorganization priorities/acceptance, the master governs global safeguards, and the adaptive policy governs visual implementation detail. Router entries and older examples are nonbinding candidates. Current official versioned docs govern APIs. Resolve conflicts explicitly and preserve validated content.

Build explanation -> verified representation -> purposeful interaction when justified -> understanding/decision. Inspect real config, routes, source exports and nested pages, components, dependencies, tokens and baseline behavior before coding. Record source IDs, audience, prerequisites, misconceptions and measurable learning objectives. Maintain source coverage and representation decisions for larger work. Inventory alone is not a full source audit.

Choose meaning and representation before library. Reuse appropriate local components, inspect current free beUI, then justify any specialist capability. For substantial visuals compare at least two viable options including a simple/no-chart solution using the adaptive policy's weighted rubric and hard blockers. Recharts/shadcn Charts, ECharts, Observable Plot, Visx, Mafs and diagram tools are candidates, not mandatory installs. Historical ADOPT/REJECT/DEFER decisions describe earlier requirements, not permanent bans.

Every teaching visual needs source ID, objective, provenance, reason for interaction, controls -> derived results, selected/rejected alternatives, keyboard/touch and text/table fallback, reset/error behavior and independent numeric/domain validation. Dynamic adaptation uses deterministic local state/responsive rules, not a runtime LLM. Motion must explain a change, connection or process. Provide reduced-motion/static alternatives, themes, mobile and relevant RTL. Label synthetic data; never fake SQL/DAX/Fabric execution.

Preserve formulas, code, media, references, deep links, question IDs/answers and saved sessions. Keep static export and assets-only hosting unless explicitly authorized otherwise. Free/open-source by default; no paid Pro, new paid backend, browser-exposed secrets or silent third-party student-data transfer. Do not access browser APIs during module evaluation/static prerender.

Proceed within authorized scope without avoidable approval checkpoints. The v2 plan does not itself authorize implementing every phase or deploying. Inspect unrelated dirty work before editing. This reference-maintenance task does not change site behavior.

## Verification and completion
Run real build/tests for implementation changes. Reference-only work uses the reference/hash/path verifier and a non-document diff check; label app/runtime QA NOT RUN if not performed. A build is not an accessibility/educational audit.
Report inventory/source coverage, affected files/routes, component/library rationale, package/service costs, PASS/FAIL/NOT RUN/BLOCKED evidence, visual/domain QA limits, caveats, rollback and next atomic task.

Reference integrity command, from repository root: `node scripts/verify-agent-reference.mjs`.

## Knowledge Atlas — documentation integration 2026-10-25
For Atlas/books/semantic learning navigation, read docs/knowledge-atlas/START_HERE.md and its repository amendment before the authoritative V1.0 master linked there. Preserve Contextual Hybrid Peek/Explorer/Guided Journey. Draw only published, evidence-reviewed semantic relations; TOC, hierarchy, membership and sequence stay separate. Reuse canonical concepts across sources and preserve all routes, IDs and progress. Renderer/library choices remain context-led under the adaptive policy. This integration authorizes preparation only, not feature implementation or deployment. Run node scripts/verify-knowledge-atlas.mjs alongside the reference verifier.

## EasyUI contextual integration - 2026-10-25
For component selection, read docs/design-system/easyui-v2/INTEGRATION_REPORT.md and docs/design-system/easyui-v2/CONTEXTUAL_COMPONENT_REGISTRY.json. Supplied V2 matrices remain upstream recommendations, not installation or QA proof. Reuse current local components first; only the native ingestion comparison pilot is implemented. Preserve Atlas semantic/publication gates; no automatic graph-engine installation or deployment. Run node scripts/verify-easyui-integration.mjs for successor integrity.
